line	<str>Talk to Gianne jnr. in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the Galarpos Mountains just east of the Poison Waste. The quickest way to travel there is by using the fairy ring code BKP and then running north-west. Alternatively, teleporting to Castle Wars via ring of dueling, then heading south-west alongside the river is also fairly quick.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a crossbow and mith grapple on the tree in the middle of the river to cross into the mountains.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Longramble.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the dying spirit tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the crystal chime on the tree. Note: Keep the Crystal chime in your inventory after this, as it needs to be in your inventory to damage the dungeon monsters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go west into the Poison Waste Dungeon entrance by entering the sewer and climbing up the ladder.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel through the dungeon until you reach a room with a pit in the centre that is connected to three other rooms.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Enter the east room and kill the three blue <col=800000>Warped Terrorbird</col>s.</col>
step	33	-	Quick guide step 33
line	<str>Talk to King Bolren in the Tree Gnome Village.</str>
line	
line	<str>Squeeze through the loose railing to the south-west, and then run east to the ladder down to the Tree Gnome Village dungeon.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run west and talk to Golrie about anti-illusion devices.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the storeroom via the tunnel in the eastern area of the dungeon.</str>
line	
line	<str>Push the monolith north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest for some discs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Push the south-west monolith north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Push the north-west monolith east.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the two chests by the northern tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>Push the small monolith south.</str>
line	
line	<str>Push the north-west monolith west.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest for the strongroom key and crystal chime seed.</str>
line	
line	<str>Click on the singing bowl to create the crystal chime from the seed. You may have to instead select the 'Sing-crystal' on the singing bowl to complete this step.</str>
line	
line	<str>Push the south-east monolith west.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the strongroom to the west.</str>
line	
line	<str>Click the book on the lectern and watch each cutscene by selecting the chapter headers. (NOTE: DROPPED ITEMS WILL DISAPPEAR AFTER THE CUTSCENE)</str>
line	
line	<str>Operate Yewnock's machine.</str>
line	
line	<str>Referencing the table to the right, insert discs on the left side of the machine to equal the values on the right side. Use Yewnock's exchanger to obtain shapes of lesser values. (NOTE: PICK UP ANY ITEMS YOU'VE DROPPED PRIOR TO CONFIRMING THE DISCS IN YEWNOCK'S MACHINE). If you are having trouble, see the full guide here.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to King Bolren and kill the evil creature.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Spirit Tree to travel to the Tree Gnome Stronghold.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the Grand Tree and climb up the ladder once.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Gianne jnr. in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the Galarpos Mountains just east of the Poison Waste. The quickest way to travel there is by using the fairy ring code BKP and then running north-west. Alternatively, teleporting to Castle Wars via ring of dueling, then heading south-west alongside the river is also fairly quick.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a crossbow and mith grapple on the tree in the middle of the river to cross into the mountains.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Longramble.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the dying spirit tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the crystal chime on the tree. Note: Keep the Crystal chime in your inventory after this, as it needs to be in your inventory to damage the dungeon monsters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go west into the Poison Waste Dungeon entrance by entering the sewer and climbing up the ladder.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel through the dungeon until you reach a room with a pit in the centre that is connected to three other rooms.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east room and kill the three blue Warped Terrorbirds.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Finish the final dialogue with Hazelmere to complete the quest.</col>
